// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! platform.resource's functions: what machine this is - the chip, its
//! clocks, where the code and the stacks are, and whether there is PSRAM -
//! and what a range of memory is to the cores.
//! A resource: no Open or Close, its first function in the first slot. The
//! base comes from OpenResource("platform.resource").
##include resources/platform as platform
##basetype PlatformBase
##name platform.resource
##bias 0
##public
/// Fill in `info` (sdk/resources/platform.zig), of which `size` bytes are
/// there - pass @sizeOf(PlatformInfo). Returns how many bytes it wrote,
/// which is the lesser of `size` and its own idea of the structure: a
/// program from the disk may have been built against another SDK than the
/// ROM answering it, so check the count before trusting a field near the
/// end. Nothing is written and 0 comes back for a `size` too small to hold
/// anything.
u32 GetPlatformInfo(*platform.PlatformInfo info, u32 size)
/// The chip's name, a C string ("ESP32-S3"). Never null.
[*:0]const u8 PlatformName()
/// The clock the system runs and times by, in Hz. It is the configured one
/// while the measurement against the crystal agrees with it (within 5%),
/// and the measured one when it does not - GetPlatformInfo's `cpu_hz` and
/// `measured_cpu_hz` are both there to be compared. What a delay loop or a
/// benchmark wants. 0 before the tick has been set up.
u32 CpuClock()
/// The kernel tick in Hz. Not timer.device's units, and not the 1/50 s
/// Delay counts in.
u32 TickRate()
/// The memory from `start`, `length` bytes, made `kind` (MEMTYPE_*) to
/// the cores: uncached, write-combining or cached. False where the
/// machine's map cannot mark it, or the chip keeps no such kinds.
bool SetMemoryType(usize start, usize length, u32 kind)
/// The core the system runs on, by its own name: what the core says of
/// itself where it can ("AMD Ryzen 7 7840HS", "ARM Cortex-A76", "SiFive
/// U74"), and the chip's core where it cannot ("Xtensa LX7"). A C string
/// of at most CPU_NAME_SIZE bytes, never null, good for as long as the
/// machine runs.
[*:0]const u8 CpuName()
/// Whether a task may use `feature` (CPUF_*): the core has the
/// instructions and the system keeps their registers across a task
/// switch. False for a number that names no feature.
bool CpuFeature(u32 feature)
/// Core `core` - 0 to one less than exec's CoreCount - into `info`
/// (sdk/resources/platform.zig), of which `size` bytes are there: pass
/// @sizeOf(CoreInfo). Returns how many bytes it wrote, as GetPlatformInfo
/// does, and 0 with nothing written for a core the system does not run
/// on.
u32 GetCoreInfo(u32 core, *platform.CoreInfo info, u32 size)
##end
